  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 339112) federal contracting shows a sharp drop in obligations for FY2026 to date. The market obligated $778M across 8,492 awards, with an average award size of $91.7K. Obligations fell 51.7% year over year. Historical context shows swings from $2.3B in FY21 to $1.6B in FY25, with FY26 to date at $778M. The Department of Veterans Affairs dominates buying, obligating $680M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense and Department of Health and Human Services follow at $42.2M and $38M respectively. SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC, FIRST NATION GROUP LLC, and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC are the top three vendors by obligations in FY2026 to date. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). This snapshot highlights concentration of spending by one buyer and by a handful of suppliers, and it signals that FY2026 to date activity is lower than recent fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the FY2026 to date drop in obligations?",
        "body": "The market obligated $778M in FY2026 to date, down 51.7% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for $680M of the total, so shifts in VA procurement strongly affect the sector. Prior fiscal years ranged from $1.1B to $2.3B, indicating volatility in year-to-year demand. Contracting volume and award counts will determine whether the FY26 shortfall persists as the year progresses."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers and suppliers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $680M. The Department of Defense obligated $42.2M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $38M. SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC received $131M, FIRST NATION GROUP LLC received $97.6M, and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC received $77.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
